DOCX: Word's linked OLE objects stay links, in and out

Word links an object to a file with o:OLEObject Type="Link" and an
external oleObject relationship. DOCX import tried to read it as an
embedded stream, failed, and kept only the preview picture; export
wrote every object as Type="Embed".
- The OOXML tokenizer hands the relationship's target to the mapper
  (ooxml:linktarget). Word writes it as file:///C:\... with
  backslashes, or as a path; either becomes a proper file URL. A
  Type="Link" object of a known kind (Excel, Word, PowerPoint ProgIDs,
  macro-enabled ones too) becomes a link object to that file, its
  filter named from the ProgID, so a missing file still links. The
  file is not read: the preview shows until the user updates links
  (0086). Other kinds keep their picture, as before; their targets
  go to the document grab bag (ElyPicturedLinks), and Writer's
  .uno:ExternalLinks lists them as "pictured", so Ely keeps such a
  file, encrypted ones too, from being saved over.
- Export writes a linked object Word knew as Type="Link" with an
  external relationship to its file, the preview kept.
- LibreOffice links whole files: a range in Word's LINK code (such as
  Rates!R1C1:R12C2) stays in the field code, but the link object
  reads the whole file; the range is not applied.

